sequenceDiagram
  accTitle: Two-tab snapshot save and conflict recovery
  accDescr: Both tabs load version n. Tab A saves successfully. Tab B submits the stale version, receives a conflict, and retains its draft until the user chooses discard and reload.
  actor U as User
  participant A as Browser tab A
  participant B as Browser tab B
  participant API as Spring Boot API
  participant DB as PostgreSQL
  Note over A,B: Same authenticated workspace, each tab has an independent draft
  A->>API: GET /api/v1/financials
  API-->>A: Snapshot version n
  B->>API: GET /api/v1/financials
  API-->>B: Snapshot version n
  U->>A: Edit and choose Save Changes
  A->>API: GET /api/v1/auth/csrf
  API-->>A: CSRF proof
  A->>API: PUT complete snapshot, expected version n
  Note over API: Authenticate session, verify CSRF and workspace membership, validate payload
  API->>DB: Begin transaction, lock current workspace snapshot
  DB-->>API: Current version n
  API->>DB: Replace active snapshot with n+1, insert audit event
  DB-->>API: Commit
  API-->>A: 200 saved snapshot
  Note over A: Synchronize server snapshot and draft baseline
  U->>B: Edit and choose Save Changes
  B->>API: GET /api/v1/auth/csrf
  API-->>B: CSRF proof
  B->>API: PUT complete snapshot, expected version n
  API->>DB: Lock and compare persisted version
  DB-->>API: Current version n+1
  Note over API,DB: Reject stale replacement, no stale write is committed
  API-->>B: 409 structured conflict
  B-->>U: Keep draft visible, offer Discard Draft and Reload
  opt User explicitly chooses discard and reload
    U->>B: Discard Draft and Reload
    B->>API: GET /api/v1/financials
    API-->>B: Latest saved snapshot
    Note over B: Replace local draft with latest snapshot, no automatic merge
  end
